.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt CMC 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm cmc
.Nd explicit-state model checker for C protocol cores
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Fl -model Ar name
.Op Fl -tlc-cfg Ar file | Fl -cfg Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value Ns Op , Ns ...
.Op Fl -inv Ar name Ns Op , Ns ...
.Op Fl -prop Ar name Ns Op , Ns ...
.Op Fl -all-props
.Op Fl -bfs | Fl -dfs Ar depth | Fl -simulate
.Op Fl -seed Ar n
.Op Fl -walks Ar k
.Op Fl -depth Ar d
.Op Fl -det
.Op Fl -max-states Ar n
.Op Fl -time Ar seconds
.Op Fl -trace-out Ar file
.Op Fl -progress Ar seconds
.Op Fl -quiet
.Op Fl -coverage
.Op Fl -clients Ar n
.Op Fl -drops Ar n
.Op Fl -dups Ar n
.Op Fl -crashes Ar n
.Op Fl -net-cap Ar n
.Op Fl -persist-cap Ar n
.Op Fl -reply-cap Ar n
.Op Fl -net Cm fifo | bag
.Op Fl -live-steps Ar k
.Nm
.Fl -replay Ar file
.Op Fl -inv Ar names | Fl -all-props
.Nm
.Fl -model Ar name
.Fl -list
.Nm
.Fl -version
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
explores every interleaving of a set of protocol nodes, the network
between them, their timers, their disk writes and their crashes, up to
the budgets given on the command line, and checks the named properties
in every state it reaches.
The nodes run the C step functions that the product itself links; see
.Xr cmc 7
for the model and
.Xr libcmc 3
for the interface a core implements.
.Pp
There is no single
.Nm
binary.
A program that uses libcmc writes a
.Fn main
that passes its table of models to
.Fn cmc_main ,
and links against
.Pa libcmc.a ;
that program is its
.Nm .
The binary built by this repository,
.Pa build/cmc ,
carries the models
.Cm hc
(the calibration core),
.Cm toy ,
and
.Cm toy-bug1
to
.Cm toy-bug3 .
.Pp
Output follows the wording of TLC, the TLA+ model checker, so the two can
be compared line by line.
Depth counts the initial state as 1.
.Ss Choosing the model and properties
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -model Ar name
The model to check, by its name in the program's model table.
Required, except with
.Fl -replay .
.It Fl -cfg Ar key Ns = Ns Ar value Ns Op , Ns ...
Core settings, passed to the core's
.Fn cfg_set .
May be given more than once; later settings override earlier ones,
including those read by
.Fl -tlc-cfg .
.It Fl -tlc-cfg Ar file
Read a TLC
.Pa .cfg
file: its
.Sy CONSTANTS
become core settings, and its
.Sy INVARIANTS
and
.Sy PROPERTIES
become the properties to check.
.It Fl -inv Ar name Ns Op , Ns ... , Fl -prop Ar name Ns Op , Ns ...
Check these properties.
The two options are synonyms; each property's kind comes from the model.
.It Fl -all-props
Check every property of the model.
.It Fl -list
Print the model's property names and exit.
.It Fl -version
Print the libcmc version and exit.
.El
.Pp
A model may mark its first properties as always checked.
At least one property must be named, or
.Fl -all-props
given.
.Ss Choosing the search
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -bfs
Breadth-first search, the default.
It finds a shortest counterexample, and its state counts are exact.
.It Fl -dfs Ar depth
Depth-first search to
.Ar depth
states.
A search that reaches the bound without finishing is reported as
incomplete, never as a pass.
.It Fl -simulate
Seeded random walks, not exhaustive.
Walk
.Va i
uses seed
.Ar n Ns + Ns Va i ;
a violation is reported with the
.Fl -seed
and
.Fl -walks Cm 1
that reproduce it.
.It Fl -seed Ar n
First seed for
.Fl -simulate .
Default 0.
.It Fl -walks Ar k
Number of walks for
.Fl -simulate .
Default 1000.
.It Fl -depth Ar d
Length of each walk, in states.
Default 100.
.It Fl -replay Ar file
Run a replay file written by
.Fl -trace-out
through the real cores, printing each state.
The model, settings and budgets are taken from the file; an option on
the command line that conflicts with the file is refused.
.It Fl -det
Determinism gate: run every step twice from copies of the same state and
fail if the two runs differ in their outputs or their next state.
.It Fl -max-states Ar n
Stop after
.Ar n
distinct states.
.It Fl -time Ar seconds
Stop after
.Ar seconds
of wall time.
.El
.Ss Choosing the environment
These options apply to message-passing cores (actor mode).
Each budget is a count over the whole run, from 0 to 255.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -clients Ar n
Client requests each node may receive.
Default 1.
.It Fl -drops Ar n
Messages the network may lose.
With
.Fl -net Cm fifo ,
a drop resets the connection and both ends are told.
Default 0.
.It Fl -dups Ar n
Messages the network may duplicate.
Needs
.Fl -net Cm bag .
Default 0.
.It Fl -crashes Ar n
Crashes, of any node.
A crash keeps any prefix of the node's pending disk writes, loses the
rest and the volatile state, resets its connections and restarts it.
Default 0.
.It Fl -net-cap Ar n
Messages in flight at once.
Default 8.
.It Fl -persist-cap Ar n
Pending disk writes per node.
Default 2.
.It Fl -reply-cap Ar n
Client replies recorded in the ghost log.
Default 8.
.It Fl -net Cm fifo | bag
.Cm fifo ,
the default, has one ordered channel per pair of nodes, as TCP does, and
never duplicates.
.Cm bag
is an unordered multiset that may duplicate.
.It Fl -live-steps Ar k
Bound, in steps of the fair schedule, for eventually-properties.
Default 1000.
.El
.Pp
Going past a cap is reported as an engine error, never silently
truncated.
.Ss Output
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -trace-out Ar file
On a violation, write the counterexample as a replay file.
.It Fl -progress Ar seconds
Print a progress line every
.Ar seconds
during breadth-first search; 0 turns it off.
Default 60.
.It Fl -quiet
Do not print the counterexample.
.It Fl -coverage
Print, for each action kind, the states it generated and the new
distinct states it found.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa *.replay
Replay files.
A header names the model, settings and budgets; each following
.Ql act
line is one action in hexadecimal, with its description as a comment.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It 0
No property was violated, and the search was complete for its mode:
breadth-first or depth-first search finished, the walks ran, or the
replay ended.
.It 1
A property was violated, an engine rule was broken (determinism,
durability, a cap), or a witness was never reached.
.It 2
Incomplete: a state, time or depth limit stopped the search before it
finished, with no violation found.
.It 3
Usage error, a bad setting, or a replay file that cannot be run.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Check every property of the toy lock server:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ build/cmc --model toy --all-props
\&...
Model checking completed. No error has been found.
\&...
49 states generated, 34 distinct states found, 0 states left on queue.
The depth of the complete state graph search is 11.
.Ed
.Pp
Find the planted bug in
.Cm toy-bug1 ,
save the counterexample, and replay it:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ build/cmc --model toy-bug1 --inv Mutex --trace-out bug1.replay
Error: Invariant Mutex is violated.
  2 clients in the critical section
\&...
$ build/cmc --replay bug1.replay --inv Mutex
.Ed
.Pp
Check a calibration configuration against its TLC result:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ build/cmc --model hc \e
    --tlc-cfg calib/hc/cfg/hc_paper_cp_n3_s1.cfg --det
.Ed
.Pp
Search a large space by random walks first:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ ./mycmc --model mymodel --all-props --crashes 1 --drops 1 \e
    --simulate --seed 7 --walks 100000 --depth 60
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libcmc 3 ,
.Xr cmc 7
.Pp
The guide and design notes:
.Lk https://gregburd.codeberg.page/libcmc/
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Greg Burd Aq Mt greg@burd.me
.Sh CAVEATS
A pass covers only the budgets given.
Raise
.Fl -clients ,
.Fl -drops
and
.Fl -crashes
until the bugs you planted are caught, and treat a run stopped by
.Fl -max-states
or
.Fl -time
as "no violation found in N states".
.Pp
.Fl -net Cm bag
allows behaviour a FIFO transport never shows, so a counterexample found
in bag mode may be spurious for a protocol that relies on FIFO order.
